{"title":"2000 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/8236f0be83c0e5299e66e9320195a065620aa0b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{23}{30}, \\frac{9}{10}, \\frac{11}{15}, \\text{and} \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" /> are written from smallest to largest then the middle fraction will be\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3dbd0f60edab82d1f303e8f75341b0f19e8d4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{23}{30} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{4}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac23 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{9}{10} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{11}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"435\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To figure out which one is the largest, we can use a common denominator for all of the fractions, and then compare the numerators.\n</p><p>First, we can find the LCM (least common multiple) of the denominators:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a905158a0cc49faf19f98f4bb48d78626232626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = 2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5a70e685a9c053ec091da649c56c1c6f14b8854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/5/e35a77f7a30724f0b082cee227411e27a6a6260a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 = 2 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecb6fe33233817abc30314d057da68dc44c9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 = 3 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e3b790b87661140619c70a7862259398c78bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Since all of the factors in the other numbers are factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we can see that the LCM of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f9945d696c70fa0c79b0d2db2cd851ec16b64b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2 \\times 10}{3 \\times 10} = \\frac{20}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a51c40b469273e0e67892746daa948c5f589240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{23}{30} = \\frac{23 \\times 1}{30 \\times 1} = \\frac{23}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c89322a2e7c98fb3229b9e9ba34e3dd3127a8aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{10} = \\frac{9 \\times 3}{10 \\times 3} = \\frac{27}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef9f713fccba7a967d13d744cdadd0284233064e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{15} = \\frac{11 \\times 2}{15 \\times 2} = \\frac{22}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58feb73ebd34c4c7a69eb891af362c4ad11525c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{4 \\times 6}{5 \\times 6} = \\frac{24}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Ordering these fractions from least to greatest, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62be90c0c1997e4d67824842db1105bb63508f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{30}, \\frac{22}{30}, \\frac{23}{30}, \\frac{24}{30}, \\frac{27}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The middle fraction is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5124ae76782266f81c97d67761dbd111241ed687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } \\frac{23}{30}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can convert the fractions to decimals, and then compare their values.\n</p><p>Using long division, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b551b5747bc67f4ea6267afb4d936461f972c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = 0.\\overline{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/981a362f5c1a05b4054b56a7791af6799ba8916b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{23}{30} = 0.7\\overline{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03ea69981fb2fed0dad7248bc5c1d815d5ef3b3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{10} = 0.9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7330f7486d5b83812802e4ebe24c27e16fc3a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{15} = 0.7\\overline{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4fc7e6a18067a2435996e2564a1b513597a4b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} = 0.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Ordering these decimals from least to greatest, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/586699ee81499fe88f1f5bef242cf9e4b18299b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{6}, 0.7\\overline{3}, 0.7\\overline{6}, 0.8, 0.9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The middle decimal is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/237d02bf65e082ccf36ed575f76f1d4230e43c59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.7\\overline{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5124ae76782266f81c97d67761dbd111241ed687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } \\frac{23}{30}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal\">2000 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\